# Smart Bookshelf API — example requests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension
# (humao.rest-client). Click "Send Request" above a request to run it.
# Requires the stack to be running: docker compose up

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

### API entry point (name, version, endpoint list)
GET {{baseUrl}}

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### List books (default: page 1, 20 per page, newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books

### List books — sorted by rating (unrated last), 3 per page, page 2
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?sort=rating&order=desc&pageSize=3&page=2

### List books — sorted by title A→Z
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?sort=title&order=asc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Search and filters (stage 4)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Search — sorted by relevance by default (title, author, publisher, ISBN, tag)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?q=clean code

### Search — typos tolerated ("clen cod" finds "Clean Code")
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?q=clen cod

### Search — Polish diacritics optional ("stanislaw" finds "Stanisław Lem")
# Solaris is not in the seed: send "Create a book" below first.
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?q=stanislaw

### Search — every word must match, possibly in different fields (needs Solaris too)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?q=solaris lem

### Search — by ISBN (hyphens, ISBN-10 or a fragment)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?q=0-13-235088-2

### Filter — several reading statuses (comma-separated or repeated keys)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?status=READING,READ&sort=title

### Filter — books currently standing on the shelf
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?location=ON_SHELF

### Filter — rated 4 or more, best first
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?minRating=4&sort=rating

### Filter — by tag (all given tags required)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?tag=programming

### Combined — search + status + rating, 5 per page
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?q=code&status=READ&minRating=4&pageSize=5

### Create a book (ISBN with hyphens is normalized to ISBN-13)
# @name createBook
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Solaris",
  "author": "Stanisław Lem",
  "isbn": "978-0-15-602760-1",
  "publisher": "Harcourt",
  "publishedYear": 2002,
  "pageCount": 204,
  "tags": ["Fiction", "Science Fiction"],
  "status": "WANT_TO_READ"
}

### Get the book created above
@bookId = {{createBook.response.body.data.id}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reading progress rules (stage 5) — run in order on the book created above
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Record progress → status becomes READING, startedAt = now
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pagesRead": 50
}

### Rate while reading (allowed for READING and READ books)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 4
}

### Reach the last page → status becomes READ, finishedAt = now
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pagesRead": 204
}

### Re-read → back to READING, progress restarts, rating kept
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "READING"
}

### Mark as READ → pagesRead = pageCount, finishedAt = now
# (an explicit "finishedAt" is also accepted, but not earlier than startedAt)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "READ"
}

### Back to the wish list → progress, dates and rating are cleared
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "WANT_TO_READ"
}

### 400 — a wish-list book cannot be rated
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 5
}

### 400 — a READ book with unread pages
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "READ",
  "pagesRead": 10
}

### Clear a nullable field (null removes the value)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "publisher": null
}

### Delete the book (204 No Content)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Error cases
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 400 — validation error (missing title, invalid ISBN checksum, rating out of range)
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "author": "Unknown",
  "isbn": "9780132350885",
  "rating": 6
}

### 400 — read-only shelf field (managed by the shelf module)
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Test",
  "author": "Test",
  "rfidUid": "04A1B2C3"
}

### 400 — pagesRead greater than pageCount
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Test",
  "author": "Test",
  "pageCount": 100,
  "pagesRead": 150
}

### 409 — duplicate ISBN (Clean Code from the seed, given as ISBN-10)
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Clean Code (duplicate)",
  "author": "Robert C. Martin",
  "isbn": "0-13-235088-2"
}

### 400 — invalid query parameter
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?pageSize=500

### 400 — unknown status value
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?status=READ,LOST

### 400 — sort=relevance without a search phrase
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?sort=relevance

### 400 — malformed id
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/not-a-uuid

### 404 — unknown id
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
